# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Test and type-check caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Market data. The repository deliberately ships none: every download lands in
# a platform cache directory outside the tree, and a 500-ticker daily universe
# over twenty years is 50-100 MB as Parquet. A stray CSV or Parquet in here is
# almost always someone's local data rather than something to publish.
.qv/
*.parquet
*.pq
*.csv

# Reports written by the tool. These are the CLI's default output directories,
# so anyone who runs `qv validate` or `qv demo` inside a clone would otherwise
# find their own audit staged for commit. The example reports under
# examples/ and real_user_tests/ are committed deliberately and are not
# matched by these patterns.
qv_report/
qv_demo/

# Credentials. Nothing in this project needs any, which is exactly why an
# .env appearing here would be an accident worth catching.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Claude Code local state. The skill source lives in skill/ and is installed
# into .claude/skills/ by `qv skill install`, so the installed copy is a build
# artifact rather than something to track.
.claude/
CLAUDE.local.md

# Editors and operating systems
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Notebooks
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Working notes. The original design document, the running session handoff and
# the internal status are how this got built, not part of what it is - they are
# kept locally and deliberately not published. STATUS.md in particular records
# where the project stands and what is left, which dates fast and would be a
# liability to publish half-true. CLAUDE.md is different and is committed: it is
# forward-looking guidance for working on the source, not a record of how the
# source came to be.
PLAN.md
PROGRESS.md
STATUS.md
